<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila says no new rules on A share purchases.</title>
<headline>Manila says no new rules on A share purchases.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine's Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) said on Tuesday it has not issued new rules allowing the purchase by foreigners of A shares whihc are exclusively for nationals, SEC executive director Eugenio Reyes said.</p>
<p>Reyes told Reuters that foreigners in theory can buy A shares through a trust fund which would still be owned by Filipinos.</p>
<p>But he added the concept is not new as it was used in the setting up of the First Philippine Fund, a mutual fund created in the late 1980's.</p>
</text>
